  "limits": "Architecture and instrument counts follow the cited Phoenix documents. Package dimensions fitted to photographs, fine routing and electronics without flight artwork remain explicitly educational. A lifted component is an inspection view, not an in-flight deployment. The extended arm uses the aluminium links and titanium end fittings shown in the JPL engineering reference, with the transport biobarrier removed. Its posture is representative, not a recovered flight command. TEGA has four paired inlets on each of two sloping faces. The individual-cell solar construction is adapted from the existing InSight inspection, with approximately 2.10 m Phoenix diameter, ten flexible gores and contact positions traced from PIA09701. The cell surface is a NEPTUNI PBR material, not a NASA photograph. Cell pitch is reconstructed, not flight artwork. The foil normal comes from NASA Eyes.",
